---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import { project, downloads, downloadUrl, verification } from '../data/project';
---
<Base title="Downloads" description="Download Scarp v0.0.5-alpha.1 for Windows x64, Linux x64, or macOS ARM64, with SHA-256 checksums and first-run instructions.">
  <section class="wrap page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Try the published alpha</p><h1>Your next experiment<br />starts here.</h1><p class="lead">Scarp v{project.version}. Choose the archive matching your operating system and CPU.</p><p class="notice">Experimental prerelease · Syntax and APIs may change.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap download-grid">{downloads.map(item => <article class="download-card"><span class="eyebrow">{item.architecture}</span><h2>{item.name}</h2><a class="button primary" href={downloadUrl(item.file)}>Download {item.file.endsWith('.zip') ? 'ZIP' : '.tar.gz'} <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="inline-link" href={downloadUrl(item.file + '.sha256')}>SHA-256 file ↗</a><details><summary>Archive checksum</summary><code class="checksum">{item.hash}</code></details></article>)}</section>
  <section class="wrap section prose"><h2>Verify, extract, run</h2><ol><li>Download the archive and its checksum file. Compare the archive’s SHA-256 digest with the published value before extracting.</li><li>Extract the whole package, including its examples directory.</li><li>Run the executable directly from that directory and confirm its version.</li></ol><h3>Linux / macOS</h3><CodeBlock filename="terminal" code={'./scarp --version\n./scarp run examples/hello.srp'} /><h3>Windows PowerShell</h3><CodeBlock filename="PowerShell" code={'./scarp.exe --version\n./scarp.exe run examples/hello.srp'} /><p>For checksum commands and source builds, follow the <a href={project.docs + 'guide/installation'}>installation guide</a>. The release publishes <a href={downloadUrl('SHA256SUMS')}>combined checksums</a> and a <a href={verification}>package verification record</a>.</p><h2>Prefer the source?</h2><p>Build the interpreter with a stable Rust toolchain and Cargo. The current language implementation has no third-party Rust crate dependencies. See the <a href={project.docs + 'guide/installation'}>source installation instructions</a>.</p><p>These packages contain an interpreter for Scarp programs. Native compilation, one-click installers, and package-manager installation channels are not advertised as available.</p></section>
  <section class="wrap prose"><h2>Need help getting started?</h2><p>The <a href="/support/#help">support hub</a> covers installation, version mismatches, silent checks, and common runtime problems. If a problem persists, <a href="/support/#report">find the correct issue tracker</a>.</p></section>
</Base>
